   271	
   272	# 2. Encoding rules bound from the start
   273	
   274	So that no recut is needed to obtain them (`s-p3/RESULTS.md:38-73`,
   275	`LEDGER.md:1264-1278`): (1) **report outputs in parallel with their
   276	continuations**, never sequential, since a synchronous output off the
   277	goal path blocks trace reconstruction (recut 1); (2) **per-role judges**,
   278	because a single event cannot say "red on exactly signer B" or "exactly
   279	layer L1", so per-slot and per-layer judge channels and events are
   280	declared from the start (recut 2); (3) **`-lib` with the shared
   281	library**, nothing redeclared, redeclaring a library term being a build
   282	failure (ENUM §1); (4) **`framed` is NOT promoted**, the seven-argument
   283	constructor copied verbatim from S-P3 as S-P1 and S-P2 copied it
   284	(`lib/tessera_theory.pvl:77-84`), with the capstone checking the copies
   285	agree; (5) **the D-1 `STMT_DIRECT` / `STMT_DIGEST` split**, the spike's
   286	single `STMT` being a build failure (`:1266-1268`); (6) **D-6's `TLR` and
   287	`REFUSAL` tags present and load-bearing under composition**, which is
   288	precisely what the capstone is for (`lib/tessera_theory.pvl:66-76`,
   289	`LEDGER.md:387-398`; see routed item 1); and (7) **the honest-flow witness is the
   290	judge's `HonestAccepted(k, fb)`**, never bare acceptance (recut 3).
