   369	## 2. Every companion, by case
   370	
   371	There is one row per configuration file. C-C1 runs in (c) only; C-C10's isolation control and C-C14 run in
   372	(a) and (b) only; every other configuration runs in (a), (b) and (d). The `rc`, seconds and peak resident
   373	set (GiB = kB / 1 048 576) are read off `ladder.log`. The box the ladder enforced is 71 100 s strict and
   374	65 700 s degraded, which is section 0's per-case-sum reading. The fourth column gives the
   375	predicted-red-box reading. **Observed reds** lists every safety query and observer that came back
   376	`is false`. In (d) that list includes the registered degraded baseline red `AcceptS => IssuerSigned`
   377	(`PREDICTIONS.md:1580`; §4 builder note (2), `:1788-1791`). A degraded companion that did not land reads
   378	**timeout (mechanism-viability failure)** or **terminated by memory guard, classified as mechanism failure
   379	(memory)**, and it has no result. *(REPAIR 2026-10-01, skeptic S-5: the second label is **the owner
   380	instance's clerk disposition**, not the registration's. The registration boxes time only — the word
   381	“memory” does not occur in `PREDICTIONS.md` — and the 80 GB rule and the classification are the owner
   382	instance's (`mem_guard_vm.sh:10-15`). Headroom at each trigger: *The degraded wave*.)*
