  1123	**How each sentence bears.** Sentence 1 sets boxes *“per run”* and gives *“each compromise case … the full
  1124	box”*; it does not distinguish correct-form runs from companions. Sentence 2 defines the full box as the
  1125	per-case sum. Sentence 3 is about companions specifically, and says both that the companions add nothing to
  1126	the total — the reason it gives — and that a companion *“runs inside the box of the query it is predicted to
  1127	red”*, naming boxes of 30 to 60 minutes. **(P), the per-case-sum reading,** takes sentence 3 as an
  1128	accounting statement (companions add no entries) and sentences 1-2 as the run limit. **(Q), the
  1129	predicted-red-box reading,** takes sentence 3's *“runs inside the box of”* as the run limit for a companion.
  1130	Neither reading makes any sentence false; they differ on which sentence sets a companion's limit.
