  1590	on C-Q1 link 2b conjunct 1**: the fourth query in declaration order, not link 2a, which lands in every
  1591	killed run (`dev/abl2a/REPORT.md` §0).
  1592	
  1593	| Companion | Case (a) | Case (b) |
  1594	|---|---|---|
  1595	| C-C7(i) `cap_cc07i` | `rc=124 seconds=71105 peakRSSkB=64988588`, timeout at the 71 100 s box (`ladder1/ladder.log:79`) | `rc=124 seconds=71105 peakRSSkB=66335336` (`:87`) |
  1596	| C-C7(ii) `cap_cc07ii` | `rc=143 seconds=25426 peakRSSkB=80131372` (`:81`), SIGTERM by the 80 GB guard (`ladder1/mem_guard_vm.log:3213`) | `rc=143 seconds=24435 peakRSSkB=80044452` (`:86`; `ladder1/mem_guard_vm.log:5621`) |
  1597	| C-C14 `cap_cc14` | `rc=143 seconds=13667 peakRSSkB=80310108` (`:80`; `ladder1/mem_guard_vm.log:2822`) | `rc=143 seconds=13186 peakRSSkB=80621176` (`:99`; `ladder1/mem_guard_vm.log:7879`) |
  1598	
  1599	The same runs had already died on wam-nuc (31 GB) at 17-31 GB (`ladder1/ladder.log:34`, `:38`, `:50`, all
  1600	`rc=137`, and `:62`, `rc=143`). §3 registers a timeout as *"mechanism-viability failure, evidence about
  1601	the tool or the encoding and **never** about the property, disposed by ablation **or a change of
  1602	tactic**"* (`PREDICTIONS.md:297-300`). This recut is that change of tactic. It is not an amendment,
  1603	because it touches no property, no query's shape and no registered prediction (§8 item 3).
  1604	
  1605	*What the setting does.* ProVerif saturates the model's Horn clauses by resolution. In each clause the
  1606	**selection function** picks the hypothesis that resolution unifies on. ProVerif 2.05's default is
  1607	`TermMaxsize`. `Term` gives every ordinary hypothesis weight 0 instead of its size, which removes the
  1608	preference for large facts (manual extract :8040 and :8047-8050, recorded in
  1609	`dev/abl2a/manual_notes.md:20-23`). The setting changes which clauses are derived on the way to the
  1610	fixpoint and how many. It changes neither the clauses the model generates nor what a query asks.
  1611	
  1612	*The soundness argument.* The ProVerif 2.05 manual, §6.6, verbatim: *"The performance settings may
  1613	result in more or fewer false attacks, but they never sacrifice soundness. It follows that when ProVerif
  1614	says that a property is satisfied, then the model really does guarantee that property, regardless of how
  1615	ProVerif has been configured using the settings presented here."* The quotation was taken from the
  1616	manual PDF on 2026-09-20 and is recorded in `dev/abl2a/manual_notes.md:6-11`. **Consequence:** under
  1617	`Term` an `is true` stays correct. The setting can cost only completeness: a false attack (`cannot be
  1618	proved`) or a slower run.
  1619	
  1620	*Why uniformly.* Applied only to the runs that died, the setting would build the tables under two
  1621	configurations (`dev/abl2a/REPORT.md:381-384`). Applied to all 80 files, every companion still differs
  1622	from its correct form by its mutation alone. The alternative was ablation step 1, which deletes the
  1623	depth-2 layer this model exists to compose. It was held in reserve for whatever still failed.
  1624	
  1625	*The controls, and what ladder 2 showed.*
  1626	
  1627	1. **Pre-ladder, isolated files** (`dev/abl2a/`, 10 GiB cap). `cap_cc09_a` with the line added reproduced
  1628	   all 47 `RESULT` lines identically (`REPORT.md:296-302`). C-C5's isolated link-2b file landed in 40 s;
  1629	   unset, it had died of memory at 949 s.
  1630	2. **Pre-ladder, full files** (`dev/recut_pre/chain.log:2-4`, 16 GiB cap). `cap_cc07ii_a` and
  1631	   `cap_cc07i_a` landed. `cap_cc14_a` reached the cap (`rc=134` at 2 798 s). **In ladder 2 it landed**:
  1632	   `rc=0`, 43 842 s, 30.8 GiB (`ladder.log:29`), and in (b) 41 473 s (`:56`).
  1633	3. **Staging smoke test** (`ladder2-staging/smoke.log:1`): 47 `RESULT` lines identical to ladder 1's
  1634	   `capstone.out`.
  1635	4. **The ladder-wide cross-check** (section *Cross-check*). All 49 files that landed in ladder 1 are
  1636	   identical byte for byte. The 7 that ladder 1 lost are prefix-consistent. There are **0 differences
  1637	   and no `cannot be proved`**, so on this suite the setting cost nothing that the cross-check can see.
  1638	
  1639	**Under ladder 2 every strict file landed**, including the three companions whose failures motivated the
  1640	recut, and case (c). The setting did **not** dispose of the degraded failures (*The degraded wave*).
  1641	
  1642	---
  1643	

