   942	  (2 418 s), but the whole file has **no admissible break point**: at step 1 the one-signer conjunct of
   943	  link 2b runs out of memory, it does so again at steps 1-2 and 1-3, and step 4 lands it only by deleting
   944	  the mutation (F1234 is identical to the ablated control). `cc05_d`'s conjunct 1 breaks only at step 4
   945	  (§(c)). Ablation also collides with C-N1. Step 1 alone kills `HonestChain(L2)`, and steps 1-4 kill six
   946	  honest-flow witnesses even in the ablated control, so any ablated run is a broken fixture under C-N1 as
   947	  frozen (§(f) items 1 and 4).
   948	- **The registration has no third disposal** (§(f) item 7). §3 registers a timeout as *"mechanism-viability
   949	  failure, evidence about the tool or the encoding and **never** about the property, disposed by ablation
   950	  or a change of tactic"* (`:297-300`).
