    59	## 0. What was built, and how the other files are derived
    60	
    61	`capstone.pv` is **the** composed model, in case **(a)** — strict, DNS channel compromised. It carries
    62	the §1.1 fixture, the §1.2 acceptance path per layer, the §1.3 events, and **every** registered query
    63	of that case in one file. The other cases and every companion are **derived from it** by
    64	`formal/suite/capstone/proverif/derive.py`, which applies named, exact-string edits inside named
    65	blocks of the model and writes a header into each generated file naming its case, what it mutates,
    66	which registered prediction it serves and the registered box. Nothing in `derive.py` edits
    67	`capstone.pv`. The delta for any generated file is therefore readable twice: in `derive.py`'s rule
    68	list, and as `diff capstone.pv <file>`.
