    11	     EXACTLY ONE key, or the script stops.
    12	  2. mkresults.py's EXPECTED held set (1) only and ignored the Cases cells, so it would mark e.g.
    13	     C-C2's strict runs (registered green) as "did not go red".  SPEC below is the per-companion,
    14	     per-case registration, read from PREDICTIONS.md §4 / §9 and cited by line.
    15	  3. assemble.py assumed one ladder and one ceiling of the ladder-1 shape.
    16	It transcribes and compares; it decides nothing.  It never reads ladder1/ for a cell: ladder 1 is
    17	read only by the cross-check (section X) and the ceiling arithmetic.
