  1081	  fixture, which is ENUM note 3's two-honest-values rule:
  1082	  `event(EstablishedWrapped(aid, lyr, t, pk(skI), core, ESTABLISHED)) ==> event(Designated(pk(skI), h(core)))`
  1083	  and the same with `pk(skI2)`. **Registered green in (a), (b) and
  1084	  (d).** These are S-STANDING Q1(ii)'s shape (`ss_q1…:224-226`).
  1085	- **Degraded (d):** the **unrestricted** form is **registered red**,
  1086	  the A4.6 cost, exactly as S-STANDING's own Q1d (i) is
  1087	  (`ss_q1d_degraded_compromised.out:640` `is false`, L-18 `:534`);
  1088	  the honest-key forms stay green (`:649`, `:658`). C-Q1's link 1b is
  1089	  not asserted in (d) for the same reason and the same amendment
  1090	  (`docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-4.md:156-171`). **A red on the
  1091	  unrestricted form in (d) is a registered cost, never a finding.**
  1092	
  1093	**Conjunct 2, the entitled key (D13).** `event StandingUnentitledWrapped(pkey, bitstring)`
  1094	over *(key the report was computed against, evidenced tuple)*, fired by
  1095	the standing path's judge when `fp(kX) ≠ kfpr`; **unreachable in
  1096	(a), (b) and (d)** — S-STANDING Q1(iii)'s shape and its registered
  1097	mode coverage (`ss_q1_strict_dns_compromised.out:530`,
  1098	`ss_q1d_degraded_compromised.out:664`).
  1099	
  1100	**What the judge observes** *(REPAIR 2026-09-17, Codex round 2
  1101	finding 1; the withdrawn clause, quoted: “fired by the standing path's
  1102	judge when `fp(kX) ≠ kfpr` **for a report carried under an `aid` that
  1103	(E1) binds to a wrapped acceptance**”)*: the judge observes **the
  1104	standing path's own report**, under the **intake** `aid` and with the
  1105	(E4) wrapped flag — exactly as SS.Q3's judge observes S-STANDING's
  1106	(`ss_q3_companionB_entitled_via_envelope.pv`, whose `StandingUnentitled`
  1107	is reachable at `cap5a_ss_q3_companionB_asis.out:860`) — and it fires
  1108	on `fp(kX) ≠ kfpr` **whether or not the envelope path accepted**. It is
  1109	therefore **reachable under C-C12**, which is what makes C-C12 a
  1110	severing of D13 at all, and **unreachable in the correct model**, where
  1111	check 7 of §1.2 rejects the unentitled key. The withdrawn clause made
  1112	the judge's reachability conditional on the very acceptance the mutation
  1113	is designed to fail.
  1114	
  1115	**Conjunct 3, scope agreement (D11's conditional half).** **ADDITION
  1116	beyond `LEDGER.md:1294`, and marked so** *(REPAIR 2026-09-17, Codex
  1117	round 3 finding 2)*. `:1294` fixes C-Q6's formulation and the rows it
  1118	consumes; it states two conjuncts and **no** scope observation. This
  1119	conjunct is **this file's**, registered here so a builder does not read
  1120	it as the ledger's.
  1121	
  1122	**Why it is added.** The round-two repair made the standing path
  1123	extract the innermost terms **itself** and consume **no** envelope
  1124	event — which is right for D13, since it is what lets C-C12 fail
  1125	(`cap11a…:1307`), and which **severs the consumption D11's conditional
  1126	half claims**. With only conjuncts 1 and 2, **nothing in C-Q6 observes
  1127	the envelope path's attribution at all**, so C-C15's scope mutations —
  1128	which change the **reported** key and leave the innermost material
  1129	untouched (`sp7_q5c_companion_one_level_in.pv:229-241`, the mutated
  1130	`out(scopeCh, …)` report at `:240`) — cannot red C-Q6, and D11's
  1131	conditional half would have had no falsifiable consumer. Conjunct 3
  1132	restores the consumption **without re-sequencing the paths**.
  1133	
  1134	**The judge, in S-P7's `ScopeJudge` house form**
  1135	(`sp7_q2_degraded_compromised.pv:349-353`, a judge over two private
  1136	channels that fires its mismatch event or its witness). The capstone's
  1137	judge reads, on private channels:
  1138	
  1139	- the **standing path's** report `(aid, lyr, kX, id)` — the key the
  1140	  standing verdict was computed against **and the innermost issuer
  1141	  identity `id`**, the first field of the `authTuple(id, kfpr, sset,
  1142	  alg, ver)` the standing path **extracted itself** under (E1); the
  1143	  path already reports `kX` for conjunct 2's judge and `id` is read off
  1144	  the same term, so no new extraction and no new check is introduced;
  1145	  and
  1146	- the **envelope path's** attribution report `(aid, lyr, kA, idA)` —
  1147	  the `scopeCh` report S-P7's models already emit — the correct
  1148	  model's at `sp7_q2_degraded_compromised.pv:303`
  1149	  (`out(scopeCh, (ctx, kI, idI, fbI))`), read by `ScopeJudge` at
  1150	  `:351`, and the **mutated** form, which reports the middle layer's
  1151	  `(kM, idM)`, at `sp7_q5c_companion_one_level_in.pv:240`.
  1152	
  1153	It fires **`ScopeMisreported(aid, lyr, kX, id, kA, idA)`** when
  1154	**`(kA, idA) ≠ (kX, id)`**, and is **registered unreachable in (a),
  1155	(b) and (d)** — the same mode coverage as conjunct 2.
  1156	
  1157	**THE COMPARISON IS OVER THE PAIR, KEY AND IDENTITY, NOT THE KEY
  1158	ALONE** *(REPAIR 2026-09-17, Codex round 4 finding 1. The withdrawn
  1159	sentence, quoted: “It fires **`ScopeMisreported(aid, lyr, kX, kA)`**
  1160	when `kA ≠ kX`, and is **registered unreachable in (a), (b) and (d)** —
  1161	the same mode coverage as conjunct 2.” The withdrawn event signature is
  1162	quoted at its declaration in §(1).)* **Why.** The inherited scope
  1163	relation D11 names covers **both** the attributed key and the
  1164	attributed issuer identity: S-P7's own judge fires
  1165	`Rescoped(kIrep, idIrep, kH, idH, fbI)` on *"an acceptance of the same
  1166	`fbI` with `(kIrep, idIrep) ≠ (kH, idH)`"* and emits
  1167	`HonestWrappedAccepted` when they are **equal**
  1168	(`s-p7/PREDICTIONS.md:226-237`). A key-only judge is strictly weaker
  1169	than the relation it is supposed to consume, and the gap is not
  1170	hypothetical: **S-P7's Q6a companion is exactly the identity-only
  1171	case** — verification under `kI` retained, the wrapper's identity
  1172	reported — and it is a **committed** companion of this suite.
  1173	
  1174	**Shown twice, in both directions.**
  1175	
  1176	- **The escape, at the reviewer's projection.** On the structural join
  1177	  with **only the reported issuer identity changed** and the key left
  1178	  alone — `cap12e_ss_q1_join_scope_identity.out` — **all three C-Q6
  1179	  conjuncts stay green**: conjunct 1 unrestricted `is true` (`:542`)
  1180	  and honest-key `is true` (`:556`), conjunct 2 `StandingUnentitled`
  1181	  unreachable (`:1368`), and the **key-only** `ScopeMisreported`
  1182	  unreachable (`:570`) — while the identity judge
  1183	  `ScopeIdentityWrong` is **reachable** (`:945`), the artifact-A /
  1184	  artifact-B substitution stays excluded (`:563`) and honest standing
  1185	  stays reachable (`:1718`). A key-only conjunct 3 therefore sees
  1186	  nothing at all where the identity alone is re-scoped.
  1187	- **The committed companion is that case.** On a copy of S-P7's own
  1188	  Q6a companion with a **key-only** scope judge added beside the
  1189	  committed full `Rescoped` query —
  1190	  `cap12f_sp7_q6a_keyjudge.out` — the key-only judge is **green**
  1191	  (`:1339`, unreachable) while the committed pair-form `Rescoped` is
  1192	  **red** (`:818` `is false`), with `HonestWrappedAccepted` (`:1130`)
  1193	  and `HonestAccepted` (`:1326`) reachable. The family's own committed
  1194	  companion is precisely what the key-only judge cannot see.
  1195	
  1196	**What does not change.** Conjunct 3 stays a **judge over two reports
  1197	the two paths already emit**; no verifier check is added, neither path
  1198	waits for the other, C-Q6's probability, residual decomposition and
  1199	90-minute timebox stand, and the conjunct remains an **ADDITION beyond
  1200	`LEDGER.md:1294`**. What changes is the **arity of the comparison**.
  1201	
  1202	**The independence is preserved, and that is the point of the judge
  1203	form.** The **judge** waits for both reports; **neither path waits for
  1204	the other**, neither path's report is conditioned on the other's
  1205	success, and no verifier check is added anywhere. The round-two
  1206	independence therefore stands and **D13's severing is not
  1207	re-shadowed**: under C-C12 the standing path still reports an
  1208	unentitled key without the envelope path's cooperation.
  1209	
  1210	**Witness.** **`HonestWrappedStandingAgreed(aid, lyr)`**, fired by the
  1211	same judge when the two reports **agree** for an honest wrapped
  1212	acceptance; **must be reachable**, on the `HonestWrappedAccepted`
  1213	pattern of `ScopeJudge`'s own `if … then` branch
  1214	(`sp7_q2_degraded_compromised.pv:352`), so that an unreachable
  1215	`ScopeMisreported` is a severing test that ran and not a judge that
  1216	never paired.
  1217	
