I found a further contract conflict in C-C15(i). BF-4 correctly makes the inner acceptance report the wrapper key it verified under, but standing still uses the separately presented inner key. The existing degraded trace shows those keys differ for the same intake and layer. That violates the registration’s “immutable” accepting-key equality; it is more than an attribution-report change. I’m checking its effect on D11 before assigning the final finding.
