  1987	  read as a lineage record's, never as a refusal record's); C-Q10 and
  1988	  C-C18 show only that the `TLR` tag check separates signing domains
  1989	  under composition. The record's
  1990	  content and decomposition (A3 §A3.7.2), the extended atomic-entry
  1991	  invariant (**L2-n**) and **E6** are neither modelled nor claimed, and
  1992	  `REFUSAL` is exercised as a signing domain and unexercised as a
  1993	  record.
  1994	- **Nothing about the adjudicator's decision.** Per A4.6 the verifier's
  1995	  job in degraded mode is to hand the adjudicator the evidence of what
  1996	  could and could not be excluded, marked degraded; a correspondence that
  1997	  holds strict and fails degraded is a registered **cost**, not a defect.
  1998	- **No absorption.** No query here may absorb an L2-a…L2-n item into a
  1999	  checked cell, treat L-14's by-construction encoding as a producer, or
  2000	  read L-01 as discharging S-P1's authorship (`:1522-1529`).
