codex
The fresh key-join probe confirms the C-C15(i) problem: envelope acceptance and standing establishment use different keys for the same intake and layer. The frozen contract says that equality is immutable.

Two other probes completed: standing can establish at an intermediate wrapper, and the wrapped witnesses can be repaired by guarding event emission without changing query signatures. The latter preserved all 47 strict-case verdicts. These affect contract fidelity and witness evidence; they do not show a baseline cryptographic attack.
