  1150	**What either choice costs.** If **(P)** governs, every severing observed in sections 2-3 stands as observed,
  1151	and the remaining gaps are those of the first question (D1, D2, D5, D10). If **(Q)** governs, five rows or
  1152	row halves (D3, D4, D6, D9, D7's membership half) have no severing shown inside its box in any case, and
  1153	three more (D7's common-content half, D8, D11) have none shown in (d); those would need either a disposal
  1154	under §3 (the registered outcome for a run that exceeds its box is a timeout, disposed by ablation or a
  1155	change of tactic) or an amendment. No re-run is proposed here: the ladder's output carries no per-query time,
  1156	and timing one query alone would need a file carrying that query alone, which is not the registered file.
