  1158	**The owner instance's recommendation (2026-10-01; a recommendation, not a ruling): (P).**
  1159	
  1160	- **Sentence 3 explains itself as accounting.** It says companions run inside a query's box *“so the
  1161	  1155-minute per-case total and the 26 entries are unchanged”*. The clause after *“so”* is the point
  1162	  being made: companions add no entries to the ceiling. Sentence 1 is the only one framed as a rule for
  1163	  runs, and it says *“per run, each compromise case getting the full box”*.
  1164	- **The builder chose (P) before any result existed.** `run_ladder.sh`'s header (2026-09-19) gives every
  1165	  file the per-case sum and records the predicted-red reading beside it. That ordering is what a frozen
  1166	  registration exists to protect: the reading was not chosen after seeing which rows it saves.
  1167	- **What (P) does not claim.** It does not claim any companion's predicted-red query finished inside 30
  1168	  to 60 minutes. Per-query time was never logged, so no reader can say. A reader who holds (Q) has a fair
  1169	  textual case. Under (Q), the record is not that eight row-halves failed; it is that they are not shown
