    22	
    23	- The revised handoff reconciled six choices as two settled construction choices plus four contestable choices; it puts the capstone claim, adversary, and limits first, calls enrollment a measurement limitation, and requires author decisions before revision/review/freeze. [Task 1]
    24	- The freeze is the author's commit containing `PREDICTIONS.md`: no capstone model may be written or run before it; afterward builders do not edit predictions, results go to `RESULTS.md`, property changes require dated amendments, and a non-author cross-family falsification review follows. [Task 1]
    25	- The routed `REFUSAL` fork is to exercise an honest refusal-tagged signer and add query/companion by amendment, or leave REFUSAL declared-but-unexercised with the composed tag property inert. [Task 1]
    26	- Verification workflow: compare every handoff claim against registration; inspect exact ranges and counts; validate staging pathspecs and changed-path coverage; state explicitly when document review ran no models. The recorded review found 17 records, 99 `cap*.pv` of 130 total models, existing staging paths, and `changed paths outside package: []`. [Task 1]

