   704	### Which box reading each severing depends on *(added 2026-10-01, REPAIR, skeptic S-4)*
   705	
   706	Section 0 records two readings of a companion's box and decides neither. **(P)**, the per-case-sum reading,
   707	gives every run the sum of its case's boxes, 71 100 s strict and 65 700 s degraded; that is what the ladder
   708	enforced, and every landed run is inside it. **(Q)**, the predicted-red-box reading, gives a companion the
   709	box of the query it is predicted to red (§3's table, `PREDICTIONS.md:1586-1595`; the assignments in words at
   710	`:1867-1876` and `:2590`). **Per-query time is not logged**: ProVerif's output carries no timestamps and
   711	`ladder.log` records one wall clock per run. A whole-run time is an upper bound on each query's, so a run
   712	that finished inside a box shows its query did; a run longer than the box shows nothing either way. Under
   713	(Q) such a run is therefore **“not shown inside its box”**, never “shown outside it”. Seconds are
   714	`ladder.log`'s (line in parentheses). Only runs that carry the row's severing, or that were the row's chance
   715	to, are listed.
